What are Connected Home Devices?
Connected home devices integrate smart technology into residential environments, enabling automation, remote control, and seamless connectivity across various household systems. These devices include smart lighting, security cameras, thermostats, voice assistants, and appliances that communicate through IoT (Internet of Things) networks. The ecosystem relies on interoperability between hardware and software platforms to enhance convenience, energy efficiency, and security for users. Platforms such as Amazon Alexa, Google Home, and Apple HomeKit serve as central hubs, enabling consumers to manage diverse devices through unified interfaces and personalized automation routines.
